# Static Linux — online ISO package list (live environment only — this is
# NOT what ends up on the installed system; that's packages/lists/*.list,
# installed live by Calamares' basepkgs/entorno-pkgs/sabores jobs).
#
# Deliberately NOT a copy of archiso's releng packages.x86_64 — releng is
# broad on purpose (it's the universal official installer: rescue tools,
# every filesystem/RAID/VPN driver under the sun). This is trimmed to what
# actually boots Static Linux's own live session and runs Calamares against
# the filesystems/bootloader this project supports.

# ---- Kernel / boot -------------------------------------------------
base
linux
linux-firmware
mkinitcpio
mkinitcpio-archiso
amd-ucode
intel-ucode
efibootmgr
memtest86+
memtest86+-efi
syslinux
grub

# ---- Filesystems / partitioning (docs/PROYECTO.md-supported set) ---------
arch-install-scripts
gptfdisk
parted
dosfstools
e2fsprogs
exfatprogs
f2fs-tools
btrfs-progs
xfsprogs
cryptsetup
lvm2

# ---- Networking (live session needs it — Calamares installs live) -
networkmanager
iwd
wpa_supplicant
modemmanager
openssh

# ---- Live GUI (bare — just enough to host Calamares) ---------------
xorg-server
xorg-xinit
openbox

# ---- Installer -------------------------------------------------------
calamares

# ---- CLI essentials (matches packages/lists/base.list) --------------
nano
vim
man-db
man-pages
less
usbutils
pciutils
rsync
reflector
pv
smartmontools
nvme-cli

# ---- Fonts (installer text) ------------------------------------------
ttf-jetbrains-mono
noto-fonts

# staticlinux-base isn't in any pacman repo yet (no Static Forge repo —
# see packages/staticlinux-base/README.md's "Future contents"), so it's
# not listed here for pacstrap. ../build.sh installs it into airootfs/
# directly by running the PKGBUILD's own package() function against the
# profile's airootfs — same tree pacstrap would produce if it were
# repo-installable, no duplicated packaging logic.
